# Windows batch files MUST be CRLF. cmd.exe parses them by byte offset, so an
# LF-only .bat breaks on labels, GOTO and parenthesised IF blocks - it runs the
# early lines, then starts executing comment text as commands ("--- is not
# recognized"). It fails in ways that look like a path or permission problem.
# Editors and tools that write LF by default reintroduced this on 11-Aug-2026.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Pine sources are opened in the TradingView editor on Windows.
*.pine text eol=crlf
